config SND_USB_OFFLOAD
	tristate "USB Audio Offload library"
	depends on SND_USB_AUDIO
	depends on USB_XHCI_HCD && USB_XHCI_SIDEBAND
	help
	  Library implementing the lifecycle of an offloaded USB audio
	  device, for a driver that owns a DSP capable of driving USB
	  endpoints. A host registers once, is told of the offload capable
	  devices as they come and go, and acquires their streams for the
	  DSP on demand.

	  Device ownership stays with snd-usb-audio: the library hooks the
	  USB-SND platform-op callbacks to pick the PCMs it can offload and
	  forward offloadable devices to the registered host.

	  The data path is built on the xHCI Audio Sideband: the library
	  claims a sideband resource for each offloaded endpoint, which makes
	  the controller route the endpoint's traffic to the DSP.

	  If unsure, say N.
